18183	{"artifactId":"PLAN-bfe98ff7f97178cf-s2","entry":{"id":"migrated-PLAN-bfe98ff7f97178cf-s2-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:controller","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-01T14:13:28.104Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"plan","stage":"plan","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"p1","ref":"s2/t1","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"openDoc's success post already contains a conditional spread of exactly the form the plan tells t1 to copy — `...(degradation !== undefined ? { degradation } : {})` — so t1's instruction to place the functionalDefinition spread 'beside the identical degradation spread already there' names a real, existing construct rather than an invented pattern.","evidence":"The pattern `degradation !== undefined ? { degradation } : {}` resolves to exactly ONE code match — docs-review-panel.ts:260 — inside openDoc's success post (the `type: 'docs-content'` at :251). So t1's instruction to place the functionalDefinition spread 'beside the identical degradation spread already there' names a real construct at a real site; the build has a line to copy rather than a pattern to invent. My probe's anchor range was a line or two short (the spread is at :260, not within :246-259), but the PLAN cites no line numbers here, so nothing in the artifact is wrong.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"p2","ref":"s2/t1","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The docs-content variant of HostToWebview currently ends at `degradation?: RenderDegradation | undefined` with `sections?: SectionIndex | undefined` immediately before it — both added additively by S001/t5 — and carries no functional-record field, so t1's 'append one optional field to this same variant, no new message type' has a real precedent and a real insertion point.","evidence":"All three reads land exactly: protocol.ts:70 `readonly type: 'docs-content