Notice, and the notice already resolves a TWO-level precedence (host-posted degradation, else the body renderer's), so t5's insertion point between stampSlugs and the chooser, and its extension of the precedence by a third level, both attach to real code.","evidence":"The pipeline is confirmed verbatim with every pattern a single match: :355 `function renderContent(m){var r=renderMarkdownBody(bodyEl,m.markdown||'');`, :362 `var stamped=stampSlugs(bodyEl,m.sections);`, :363 `renderSectionChooser(secEl,stamped>0?m.sections:{anchors:[]},jumpToSection);` and :366 `renderDegradationNotice(noticeEl,(m.degradation&&m.degradation.degraded)?m.degradation:r.degradation);`. t5's insertion point (between :362 and :363) is a real position, and the two-level notice precedence it extends by one level is visible at :366 — so 'a strict extension, not a replacement' is accurate.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"p13","ref":"s2/t6","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The S001 test t6 is told to REWRITE really exists and really asserts what the plan says: it checks `export type StructuredRenderer<` is present in docs-review-panel.ts, then loops the four named files asserting `doesNotMatch(src, /:\\s*StructuredRenderer</)` — so t6 is narrowing a live assertion, not deleting a dead one.","evidence":"The test t6 rewrites is live and asserts exactly what the plan says: test:433 `assert.match(panel, /export type StructuredRenderer</, ...)`, :436 the loop over `['docs-review-panel.ts', 'docs-review-client.ts', 'docs-sections.ts', 'markdown-style.ts']`, and :438 `assert.doesNotMatch(src, /:\\s*StructuredRenderer</, ...)`. t6 is narrowing a live assertion at its first implementer, not deleting a dead one, and the four file names in the plan match the four in the loop.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"auto"},{"claimId":"p14","ref":"s2/t2","kind":"inventory","severity":"LOW","premise":"The single markup-injection site the plan promises to